WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:05.080
Filmgoers have finally discovered something
Deadpool's longtime comics fans have known

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:08.780
for a while: the Merc with a Mouth is nearly
impossible to kill.

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:13.969
He soaks up bullets, survives buildings burning
down, and even regrows a hand in the weirdest

00:00:13.969 --> 00:00:14.969
way possible.

00:00:14.969 --> 00:00:18.890
“Am I crazy, or is your hand really small?”

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:21.400
“About the size of a KFC spork.”

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:25.369
It's easy to leave the theater wondering exactly
how anyone could ever defeat someone with

00:00:25.369 --> 00:00:27.210
such an amazing healing factor.

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:31.380
Fortunately, years of Deadpool comics have
offered an array of techniques for accomplishing

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:32.529
just such a goal.

00:00:32.529 --> 00:00:34.620
Supervillains, avert your eyes!

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:37.330
Here are just a few ways to defeat Deadpool.

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:38.609
It takes a planet

00:00:38.609 --> 00:00:43.190
Like most Marvel characters, Deadpool has
died in the comics, and in a pretty staggering

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:44.550
variety of ways.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:49.970
He recently bit the big chimichanga in Deadpool
#45… when an entire planet fell on him.

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:53.609
Which isn't too out of line for a normal Deadpool
adventure anyhow.

00:00:53.609 --> 00:00:58.010
Deadpool was just one of many casualties during
Marvel's latest Secret Wars event, in which

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:01.879
different parallel worlds collide with each
other, with the intention of thinning out

00:01:01.879 --> 00:01:06.020
the complicated multiverse and making Marvel
Comics a bit more reader-friendly.

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:10.410
By the end of the story, there are just two
parallel Earths — the one we know and love,

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:13.800
and Marvel's Ultimates Earth, which smack
into one another.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:18.570
Like most comic book deaths, this was a temporary
arrangement, as Mr. Fantastic and his family

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:22.600
eventually helped recreate the entire multiverse,
Deadpool included.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:26.450
The event certainly cements that there are
some things even Deadpool's healing factor

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:29.320
can't take on… like reality falling apart.

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:30.460
Take away his powers

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:34.770
Deadpool's main thing is his impressive mutant
healing factor, which allows him to bounce

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:36.540
back from nearly anything.

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:41.020
Without the ability to regrow body parts,
he's just a guy with a lot of weapons, a very

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:43.590
sick human body, and no sense of self-preservation.

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:46.400
So, how can you steal Deadpool's mojo?

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:47.980
“I’m gonna get ya!

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:49.560
I’m gonna get ya!

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:51.150
Ah shakin’ my milkshake!”

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:55.450
When it comes de-powering super-people, there
are a surprising number of options.

00:01:55.450 --> 00:02:00.270
Scarlet Witch notably stripped most mutants
of their powers during Marvel's House of M

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:04.180
event, but if you don't want the nuclear option,
there's always the mutant Leech.

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:08.850
As his unfortunate name implies, Leech has
the ability to effectively turn off the powers

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:11.319
of nearby super-humans and mutants.

00:02:11.319 --> 00:02:15.819
If Deadpool were in the same general area
as Leech, he could be killed just like a regular

00:02:15.819 --> 00:02:20.790
person, providing you could get past the dozens
of machine guns and swords he usually carries.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:22.040
Yea, good luck with that.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:27.200
He also barely escaped death when confronting
the Walrus, a villain with a magic, power-cancelling

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.200
hammer.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:32.989
So, where physical violence will usually fail,
a little bit of magic goes a long way.

00:02:32.989 --> 00:02:33.989
Science!

00:02:33.989 --> 00:02:36.980
If you don't want to rely on superpowers,
there's also science.

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:41.560
The answer could be as simple as the special
serum used in Deadpool #54, which made him

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:44.189
handsome, but also took away his healing factor.

00:02:44.189 --> 00:02:46.760
Don't have access to a chemistry set?

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:48.239
Carbonadium is also an option.

00:02:48.239 --> 00:02:52.970
Like vibranium and adamantium, carbonadium
is another fictional Marvel metal that villains

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:56.409
like Doctor Octopus and Omega Red have used
over the years.

00:02:56.409 --> 00:03:00.780
It's one of the reasons Omega Red is such
a deadly foe for Wolverine: his radioactive

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.739
tentacles are able to negate Logan's healing
factor.

00:03:03.739 --> 00:03:08.139
While Deadpool hasn't felt the deadly sting
of carbonadium himself, a Deadpool from a

00:03:08.139 --> 00:03:12.900
parallel universe used some carbonadium katanas
as he killed every living hero.

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:17.230
The swords were able to successfully decapitate
Wolverine and turn off his healing factor

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:18.870
— so no one is safe.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:20.499
Cure his cancer

00:03:20.499 --> 00:03:24.760
The sad truth is that without his hyperactive
healing powers, Deadpool would have already

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:27.159
died from especially aggressive cancer.

00:03:27.159 --> 00:03:31.040
Fortunately, his healing factor is in harmony
with the disease, helping him to grow new

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:35.340
cells at the exact rate that he loses them,
even though it doesn't really fix his freaky

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:36.340
face.

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:41.109
As a result, Deadpool's level of healing seems
to be a bit above the usual Wolverine levels.

00:03:41.109 --> 00:03:46.180
This was demonstrated in a rather grisly way
when a group of Skrulls decided to steal Deadpool's

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:48.819
powers for themselves... but didn't steal
his illness.

00:03:48.819 --> 00:03:53.549
That meant that their bodies were healing
way too much, way too fast, causing the Skrull

00:03:53.549 --> 00:03:57.290
warriors to become swollen and deformed until
they exploded.

00:03:57.290 --> 00:04:01.069
Theoretically, the same thing would happen
to Deadpool if any enterprising villain were

00:04:01.069 --> 00:04:02.549
able to cure his cancer.

00:04:02.549 --> 00:04:04.390
It's just too much of a good thing.

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:05.939
Give him the feels

00:04:05.939 --> 00:04:10.959
Despite often being written as an insane and
violent parody, one consistent quality Deadpool

00:04:10.959 --> 00:04:14.680
has is that he forms strong bonds with friends,
teammates, and kids.

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:18.230
Who else could have formed a rapport with
Negasonic Teenage Warhead?

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:19.940
“You, Chicken Noodle.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:21.720
Nothing compares to you.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:22.720
Sinead O’Connor.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:23.720
1990.

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:24.720
Sorry.”

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:25.720
“That’s alright.

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:26.720
You’re cool.”

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:30.600
That bonding with young people is rooted in
the comics as well, with Deadpool forming

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:34.240
a protective relationship with Evan, a young
clone of Apocalypse.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:36.050
What does this have to do with defeating Deadpool?

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:40.830
Well, in true comics tradition, he's just
like every other hero; he's easily manipulated

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:42.620
when it comes to people he cares about.

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:45.100
“WHY DID YOU SAY THAT NAME!?”

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:48.790
Deadpool was willing to risk his own life
in order to redeem Evan and stop him from

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:51.020
going down the dark path of Apocalypse.

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:54.050
All it takes is a little emotional leverage
to defeat Deadpool.

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:58.200
A broken heart might not kill him, but it
would totally keep him out of action for a

00:04:58.200 --> 00:04:59.200
while.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:00.280
Heroes and Villains

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:04.720
Even before a planet was dropped on him, both
good guys and bad guys have actually been

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:06.510
defeating Deadpool for years.

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:09.580
Thanos is one of the biggest villains in the
Marvel Universe.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:13.790
Even when he isn't wielding the Infinity Gauntlet,
he's able to obliterate characters that are

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:15.660
otherwise really difficult to kill.

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:20.380
Wasting no time, Thanos kills Deadpool on
the second page of the four-issue Deadpool

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:22.420
vs. Thanos miniseries.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:26.420
Deadpool is legitimately dead… until he's
brought back to life by Death herself, who,

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:28.170
of course, has a crush on Deadpool.

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:31.890
And that's not even the last all-powerful
opponent that tangled with Wade.

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:35.640
Loki was actually able to defeat Deadpool
in the most bizarre way possible.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:39.840
Forget about magic and powerful Asgardian
weapons, which would probably do a good job

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:41.870
cutting Deadpool down to size.

00:05:41.870 --> 00:05:46.650
Loki's curse results in Deadpool being annoyed
by almost everything in his life, and the

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:50.080
creation of possibly the best Deadpool costume
of all time.

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:54.930
And as a twisted bonus, the curse also prevents
Deadpool from killing himself whenever he

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:55.930
tries.

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:57.870
It's crazy, even for Deadpool.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:02.470
The potential to defeat Deadpool seems to
lie in the hands of any number of Marvel characters.

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:07.030
The Sentry, with his Superman-level strength
and his willingness to kill, has a reputation

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:11.350
for throwing people into the sun, which Deadpool
probably wouldn't be able to recover from.

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:15.890
Mister Fantastic is known for trapping people
in inescapable pocket universes.

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:21.090
Molecule Man can control matter at an atomic
level, and a Deadpool without atoms is no

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:22.090
Deadpool at all.

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:25.360
And we're not saying that Squirrel Girl can
defeat just about anyone….

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:26.650
But Squirrel Girl.

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:31.120
"All I see are squirrels!

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:35.540
Horrible Horrible Squirrels!"

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:36.400
Thanks for watching!

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:39.180
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:41.490
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

